# LATRA CLIENT RECORDS SYSTEM - PROFESSIONAL PRODUCT BUILD PROMPT

## 1. Product Goal

Build a simple, efficient, multi-tenant LATRA client records and renewal tracking system for tenant companies that help customers process LATRA-related services.

Priorities:
- daily usability
- fast data entry
- clear records
- renewal follow-up efficiency
- tenant data isolation
- role-based access
- simple but professional UI
- maintainable Django architecture

The product helps tenants manage:
- customers served
- customer phone numbers, when available
- brokers or agents who brought customers
- broker phone numbers
- plate numbers
- vehicle category
- LATRA service records
- issue dates
- expiry dates
- reminders
- editable WhatsApp follow-up messages

## 2. Technology And Architecture

Use:
- Django
- PostgreSQL
- Tailwind CSS
- Django templates
- modular monolith architecture

Recommended apps:
- accounts
- tenants
- customers
- brokers
- vehicles
- latra
- reminders
- dashboard
- audit

Do not use microservices for MVP.
Do not mix Bootstrap and Tailwind.

## 3. Multi-Tenancy Rules

Every business record belongs to one tenant.

Tenant-scoped models:
- Customer
- Broker
- Vehicle
- LatraRecord
- ReminderLog
- UserVehiclePermission
- AuditLog

Rules:
- never expose cross-tenant data
- never trust `tenant_id` from forms
- derive tenant from authenticated user context
- tenant-filter every query

## 4. Roles And Access

Roles:
- Admin
- Manager
- Receptionist

Admin can:
- manage users
- assign vehicle categories
- manage all records
- view reports
- manage tenant settings

Manager can:
- view reports
- manage records
- monitor staff activity
- access assigned categories or all categories depending on permission

Receptionist can:
- add customers
- add brokers
- add vehicles
- add LATRA records
- view expiry reminders
- generate and edit WhatsApp follow-up messages
- not hard-delete important records

## 5. Vehicle Category Permission Rules

Supported categories:
- CAR
- MOTORCYCLE
- BAJAJI
- OTHER
- ALL

Permission enforcement must affect:
- vehicle lists
- customer vehicle records
- LATRA records
- dashboard counts
- expiry reminders
- WhatsApp follow-up lists
- reports

Do not enforce this only in the UI. Enforce it at query and service level.

## 6. Core Data Rules

Customer:
- phone number is optional
- broker is optional
- customer can have many vehicles
- customer can have many LATRA records

Broker:
- can bring many customers
- reports must include total customers, active customers, expiring records, expired records
- no commission or payment logic in MVP

Vehicle:
- minimal MVP fields
- use unique `tenant + plate_number`
- vehicle can have many LATRA records

LATRA service:
- use free-text `service_name`
- do not hard-code service choices in MVP

LATRA record:
- validate `expiry_date >= issue_date`
- preserve expired record history
- do not overwrite old renewal history
- renewal should create a new record and preserve prior data

## 7. Reminder And Contact Rules

Contact logic:
- if customer phone exists, contact customer
- else if broker phone exists, contact broker
- else mark contact as missing

Reminder windows:
- 30 days before expiry
- 7 days before expiry
- expiry today
- already expired

WhatsApp MVP:
- use click-to-chat only
- generate default message
- let the user edit the message before opening WhatsApp
- URL-encode the final message
- do not send automatically

## 8. UX And Engineering Rules

UX principles:
- receptionist speed
- low training requirement
- simple forms
- clear tables
- visible actions
- mobile-friendly pages
- searchable records
- fast follow-up workflow

Tailwind UI expectations:
- reusable partials for buttons, inputs, cards, badges, tables, modals, alerts, empty states, pagination
- avoid repeating giant utility strings
- keep the interface office-friendly and practical

Engineering rules:
- keep business logic out of templates
- use services for expiry calculation, contact selection, WhatsApp generation, permission filtering, LATRA create and renew flows, and broker statistics
- use server-side validation
- require login
- preserve audit metadata
- no hard delete for important records
- prefer clarity over cleverness

## 9. Query And Reporting Rules

All list pages should support:
- search
- filter
- pagination

Key filters:
- customer
- broker
- plate number
- vehicle category
- service name
- expiry status
- date range

MVP dashboard and reports should include:
- total customers
- total brokers
- total vehicles
- active LATRA records
- expiring in 30 days
- expiring in 7 days
- expiring today
- expired records
- customers per broker
- active customers per broker

## 10. Out Of Scope

Do not build unless explicitly requested:
- broker commission
- payment system
- document uploads
- WhatsApp Cloud API
- SMS gateway
- mobile app
- customer portal
- LATRA government API integration
- advanced AI features
- accounting module

## 11. MVP Build Order

Build in this order:
1. authentication
2. tenant model and isolation
3. roles
4. vehicle category permissions
5. broker management
6. customer management
7. vehicle management
8. LATRA record management
9. expiry status calculation
10. dashboard
11. expiring and expired lists
12. editable WhatsApp flow
13. broker reports
14. basic audit trail
15. UI polish
